          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called the
            %em 21cm hydrogen line
            or just
            %em hydrogen line
            is the signature of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+radiation"} electromagnetic radiation
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavelength"} wavelength
            about 21
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cm"} cm
            which is emitted by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hydrogen"} hydrogen
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atoms"} atoms
            when the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            in their shell change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            from the “triplet” to the singlet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+state"} ground state
          %h2#in_astrononmy In astrononmy
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/astronomy"} astronomy
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tully-Fisher+relation"} Tully-Fisher relation
            is a relation between the asymptotic behaviour of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/galaxy+rotation+curves"} galaxy rotation curves
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/21cm+hydrogen+line"} 21cm hydrogen line
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryonic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/galaxies"} galaxies
          %h2#in_cosmology In cosmology
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
            it has been argued (
            %a{:href => "#HiganRees79"}> Higan-Rees 79
            ) that observation of a absorption at the 21cm hydrogen line in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+microwave+background"} cosmic microwave background
            would be a signal from the time when the first
            %span.newWikiWord
              stars
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/stars"} ?
            formed and ignited, a cosmological epoch not otherwise accessible to observation. A claim of detection of this signal by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/EDGES"} EDGES
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            appeared in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BRMMM18"} BRMMM 18
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrogen_line"} Hydrogen line
            %li
              %p
                Hyperphysics,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://hyperphysics.phy-astr.gsu.edu/hbase/quantum/h21.html"} The Hydrogen 21-cm line
          %h3#ReferencesInAstrophysicsAndCosmology In astrophysics and cosmology
          %p
            The suggestion that the 21cm hydrogen absorption line in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+microwave+background"} cosmic microwave background
            should be an interesting probe for early universe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
            goes back to
          %ul
            %li#HiganRees79
              C. J. Hogan,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Rees"} Martin Rees
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Spectral appearance of non-uniform gas at high
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/188.4.791"} doi:10.1093/mnras/188.4.791
          %p Review includes
          %ul
            %li#PritchardLoeb11
              %p
                Jonathan Pritchard, A. Loeb,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 21 cm cosmology in the 21st century
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1109.6012"} arXiv:1109.6012
            %li
              %p
                Jonathan Pritchard,
                %em Cosmological probes of inflation and the 21 cm line
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.perimeterinstitute.ca/videos/cosmological-probes-inflation-and-21-cm-line"}> video recording
                )
            %li#Zaroubi12
              %p
                Saleem Zaroubi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Epoch of Reionization
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The First Galaxies
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1206.0267"} arXiv:1206.0267
          %p
            A claim of detection of the cosmological signal by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/EDGES"} EDGES
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#BRMMM18
              %p
                Judd D. Bowman, Alan E. E. Rogers, Raul A. Monsalve, Thomas J. Mozdzen, Nivedita Mahesh,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An absorption profile centred at 78 megahertz in the sky-averaged spectrum
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.nature.com/articles/nature25792"} doi:10.1038/nature25792
            %li
              %p
                Raul A. Monsalve, Bradley Greig, Judd D. Bowman, Andrei Mesinger, Alan E. E. Rogers, Thomas J. Mozdzen, Nicholas S. Kern, Nivedita Mahesh,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Results from EDGES High-Band: II. Constraints on Parameters of Early Galaxies
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.07774"} arXiv:1806.07774
          %p Discussion incluces
          %ul
            %li#Falkowski18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+Falkowski"}> Adam Falkowski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://resonaances.blogspot.fr/2018/03/21cm-to-dark-matter.html"} 21cm to dark matter
          %p Calling this argument into question:
          %ul
            %li
              Richard Hills, Girish Kulkarni, P. Daniel Meerburg, Ewald Puchwein,
              %em Concerns about Modelling of the EDGES Data
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.01421"}> arXiv:1805.01421
              )
          %p
            Arguments that this detection of the 21cm line rules out substantial contributions of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+dark+matter"} fuzzy dark matter
          %ul
            %li#Nebrin17
              %p
                Olof Nebrin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmic Dawn in a Fuzzy Universe: Constraining the nature of Dark Matterwith 21 cm Cosmology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.diva-portal.org/smash/record.jsf?pid=diva2%3A1195402&dswid=-8037"} diva2:1195402
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://su.diva-portal.org/smash/record.jsf?pid=diva2%3A1195402&dswid=6755"} urn:nbn:se:su:diva-154861
            %li#NebrinGharaMellema18
              %p
                Olof Nebrin, Raghunath Ghara, Garrelt Mellema,
                %em Fuzzy Dark Matter at Cosmic Dawn: New 21-cm Constraints
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.09760"}> arXiv:1812.09760
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.reddit.com/r/Physics/comments/a9zeeb/my_first_paper_fuzzy_dark_matter_at_cosmic_dawn/"} reddit
        .revisedby
          %p
